║  Smoke: python3 bin/individuals.py ALL.chr1.tiny.vcf 1 0 300 300 ║
║  Flags: PURE PYTHON WORKFLOW, NOTHING TO COMPILE. Use the Python annotation path (dftracer-annotate-python), not clang. Do NOT install or use Pegasus, Condor or PMC: the bin/ task scripts run standalone and that is all this smoke needs. SCOPE: annotate bin/individuals.py only -- it is ~82% of workflow wall time; its VCF read loop and its per-individual file-write + tar-compress path are where the I/O is. DFTRACER VERSION: after installing, check the installed version (pip show dftracer) and REPORT it. It must be a real release version -- a 0.0.x version means the clone lost its git tags and is not the requested build; fix and reinstall rather than continuing. The input is staged READ-ONLY at /p/lustre3/haridev/1kg-eval/data and holds ALL.chr1.tiny.vcf (300 VCF data rows) plus columns.txt, which individuals.py reads from its WORKING DIRECTORY. Copy those two into the run directory; do not modify the staged copies. THE RUN IS ONLY SUCCESSFUL IF IT PRODUCES A DFTRACER TRACE that covers the I/O: a .pfw or .pfw.gz must exist afterwards and you must report its path, size and EVENT COUNT, and the event count must reflect the per-individual write path, not just one span per function. A run that exits 0 but writes a trace with a handful of events has not captured the I/O. ║
