ompile):\n\nSTEP 1 (already answered by the args above — just print \"Starting pipeline for 1000genome-workflow @ master\" and move on).\n\nSTEP 2 — SESSION SETUP:\n  a. session_create(url=APP_URL, ref=REF) → get RUN_ID, WS. Get canonical paths via session_get_run_paths — never hand-build paths like \"ws/build_ann\".\n  b. mcp__dftracer__profile_bind right after session_create succeeds.\n  c. This is a pure Python app with no compiled build step — session_detect should report build_tool=python (or none/script). Do NOT run cmake/configure steps. If session_configure/session_build_install are required by the tool flow for a python project, call them; otherwise skip straight to installing dftracer.\n  d. session_install_dftracer(run_id=RUN_ID) — must land dftracer in the SAME venv the app will run in. After it succeeds, `pip show dftracer` in that venv and REPORT the version; if it's 0.0.x, treat as a failure, fix (likely the dftracer clone lost git tags — reinstall from the correct source/tag) and retry.\n  e. session_copy_annotated(run_id=RUN_ID) — copies source into annotated/.\n  f. session_validate_structure(run_id=RUN_ID); if clean=false, session_reorganize_structure(run_id=RUN_ID, dry_run=False) then re-validate.\n\nSTEP 3 — ANNOTATION (Python path only, bin/individuals.py only):\n  Use mcp__dftracer__python_annotate_project or python_annotate_file (or dispatch via the Agent tool to the \"dftracer-annotate-python\" subagent with model=\"sonnet\" — prefer this dispatch since it is specialized) scoped to bin/individuals.py in the annotated/ tree. Make sure the VCF read loop and the per-individual write+tar-compress path both get instrumented (likely multiple functions/call sites, not just the top-level main). Follow the Python annotation rules from the skill you loaded (no @staticmethod log_static, no numba/torch.jit decorators, no __len__ — not applicable here but keep in mind for any similar traps). Use python_extract_functions / python_estimate_function_cost as