{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TAZsTtvMghPyod6E1866zh","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Detected system: **corona** (from hostname `corona82`)\\n\\n## System: corona\\n**Corona HPC system with Intel classic toolchain, MVAPICH2, and Flux wrapper launchers**\\n- sudo available: False\\n- MPI launcher: `flux run`\\n\\n### Modules (load in order)\\n  1. StdEnv\\n  2. intel-classic/2021.6.0-magic\\n  3. mvapich2/2.3.7\\n  4. flux_wrappers/0.1\\n\\n### Notes\\nDetected from hostname corona82. Application launch scripts use flux/flux_wrappers rather than bare mpirun. Load Lmod init before module operations; use the app's own scripts as the source of truth for exact module/env setup on this system.\\n## Tracing features (probed on this node)\\n\\n### PAPI hardware counters\\n  version: 5.6.0.0  (module: `not pinned`)\\n  prefix: `/usr`\\n  **hardware counters: 5** — 26 presets are listed, but only this many fit at once;\\n  ask for more and PAPI time-shares them and reports scaled estimates, with a zero exit code.\\n  derived presets (cost >= 2 counters each): PAPI_TLB_IM, PAPI_L1_ICH, PAPI_L1_TCA\\n\\n  components:\\n    - `perf_event` enabled — Linux perf_event CPU counters\\n    - `perf_event_uncore` DISABLED — No uncore PMUs or events found\\n    - `appio` enabled — \\n    - `coretemp` enabled — Linux hwmon temperature and other info\\n    - `example` enabled — A simple example component\\n    - `infiniband` enabled — Linux Infiniband statistics using the sysfs interface\\n    - `lmsensors` enabled — lm-sensors provides tools for monitoring the hardware health\\n    - `lustre` DISABLED — No lustre filesystems found\\n    - `micpower` DISABLED — Cannot read /sys/class/micras/power\\n    - `mx` DISABLED — No MX utilities found\\n    - `net` enabled — Linux network driver statistics\\n    - `rapl` DISABLED — Not an Intel processor\\n    - `stealtime` enabled — Stealtime filesystem statistics\\n\\n### PAPI counters for code_type=`io`\\n  NOTE: CPU presets cannot see I/O. Use dftracer's POSIX/HDF5/MPI-IO tracing. The cycles group is included only as a control.\\n  - **cycles** — Wall-clock anchor and IPC denominator; the baseline for everything else.\\n    PAPI_TOT_CYC, PAPI_TOT_INS\\n\\n  Partitioned into 1 run(s) against a budget of 5 (native=1, derived>=2 (ESTIMATE — verify with args.multiplex)):\\n    run 1 (est. cost 2/5): `DFTRACER_PAPI_EVENTS=PAPI_TOT_CYC,PAPI_TOT_INS`\\n\\n  VERIFY: For every run, read args.multiplex back out of the trace: 0 = exact hardware counts, 1 = time-shared estimates (do not quote those as measurements). Also compare the PAPI_* keys that actually landed in args against DFTRACER_PAPI_EVENTS — dftracer drops a preset it cannot fit rather than reporting nonsense, so a run can succeed with fewer counters than requested.\\n\\n### Node power\\n  - gpu: `rocm_smi` (/opt/rocm-7.2.1) — GPU package power via variorum's rocm_smi domain\\n  - cpu: `rapl_powercap` (/sys/class/powercap/intel-rapl) — CPU/package energy via the powercap sysfs interface\\n  - cpu: `msr` (/dev/cpu/0/msr) — variorum's MSR path; needs read permission on the msr device\\n  **ENABLE IT** — session_detect features: variorum=True, variorum_build=ALWAYS, rocm_path_for_variorum=/opt/rocm-7.2.1\\n  ! Variorum is SERVICE-SIDE only — it is sampled by dftracer_service, never linked into the traced application. A dftracer that puts it in the global DEPENDENCY_LIB drags librocm_smi64 into the app and corrupts the heap at exit (fixed upstream; verify with `ldd` on the instrumented binary if apps start aborting in __run_exit_handlers).\\n  ! DFTRACER_BUILD_VARIORUM=ALWAYS: an already-installed variorum is usually built for none of this machine's power domains and fails at init with _ERROR_VARIORUM_UNSUPPORTED_PLATFORM.\\n  ! rocm_path_for_variorum is the NEWEST ROCm on this node, which is not necessarily the one the app was built against. When a session has an app-matched ROCm (session_detect's features.rocm.path), that one wins — two rocm_smi ABIs in one process is the failure mode above.\\n\\n### Recommended session_detect features\\n  - `variorum` = True\\n  - `variorum_build` = ALWAYS\\n  - `rocm_path_for_variorum` = /opt/rocm-7.2.1\\n  - `papi_supported` = True\\n  - `papi_hardware_counters` = 5\\n  - `papi_events` = ['PAPI_TOT_CYC', 'PAPI_TOT_INS']\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZ2Pc1CmgVMYTPSkxn2Qm5","session_id":"afb86d9e-6ad6-45f6-ad84-a569d8db98ea","uuid":"9b3a4565-4bee-4037-8bce-9320dbadbc18","timestamp":"2026-09-15T23:58:10.205Z","tool_use_result":{"_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}}},"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"1000genome dftracer pipeline STEP 1-7"}
